%% alt: Difference between sessions and JWT — with sessions, the server remembers user info in a session store and the user carries only a ticket number, but with JWT, the information is held in the token itself, so the server stores nothing and only verifies the signature
flowchart LR
  subgraph JWT["JWT — The server doesn't remember"]
      direction LR
    JB["Browser<br/>Holds token (with info)"] --> JS["Server"]
    JS --> JV{"Verify signature only"}
    JV -.->|"No storage · Any server OK"| JS
  end
  subgraph SESS["Session — The server remembers"]
      direction LR
    SB["Browser<br/>Holds only session ID (ticket)"] --> SS["Server"]
    SS --> SD[("Session store<br/>abc123 → Kim Chulsoo")]
    SD -.->|"Needs sharing across multiple servers"| SS
  end
  JWT ~~~ SESS
